# A missing file must answer 404, not the whole app shell.
#
# Cloudflare Pages answers any path it cannot find with index.html, so the
# client-side router can pick it up. That is right for /player and
# /community, and wrong for a picture that is not there: the browser would
# download 306 KB of markup to try to decode as an image. Three references
# did exactly that.
#
# So the asset extensions answer 404 on their own. A real file at one of
# these paths is still served normally - Pages looks for the file first.
/*.png 404
/*.jpg 404
/*.jpeg 404
/*.webp 404
/*.gif 404
/*.svg 404
/*.ico 404
/*.mp3 404
/*.wav 404
/*.woff 404
/*.woff2 404
